// Build config for the PUBLISHED package.
//
// `npm run build` compiles everything, because the owner's local install needs
// the private facades. `npm run build:dist` — which `prepack` runs — compiles
// this instead, and it omits them.
//
// The four excluded modules are private: senken and mother read a live trading
// Postgres, deck reads a personal Supabase, terminal holds wallet credentials.
// They were shipping to npm as compiled JS *and source maps* through 2.1.4, so
// a public install carried recoverable source for tools it could never use.
// The visible symptom was the one that mattered: users saw facades they had no
// way to enable.
//
// Excluding at build time rather than filtering at publish time is deliberate.
// A denylist in package.json `files` is a thing someone has to remember to
// update when a fifth private facade appears; an absent build output cannot be
// forgotten. tools/index.ts imports these dynamically and tolerates the
// failure, and the kernel only registers an app facade whose tools actually
// resolved — so the public build has no path to them at all.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": [
    ".decibel",
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "src/tools/senken.ts",
    "src/tools/deck.ts",
    "src/tools/mother.ts",
    "src/tools/terminal.ts"
  ]
}
